## SECTION 7 — RAG Usage Validation

| Question | Finding |
|---|---|
| **Where is RAG used?** | [rag.py](file:///Users/vaxdsav/lignuaverse/backend/rag.py) `build_context()` → feeds into [agent.py](file:///Users/vaxdsav/lignuaverse/backend/agent.py) `parse_intent()` |
| **Is it real RAG (vector retrieval)?** | **No.** It's direct SQL → text context injection. This is **context grounding**, not RAG with embeddings/vector search. |
| **Is this justified?** | **Yes.** For a single-shop MSME inventory (5–500 items), full context dump is simpler and more accurate than vector similarity search. |
| **Hallucination pathways** | 1. LLM could hallucinate SKUs not in context (mitigated by system prompt instruction #2). 2. If context is too large (§3.2), the LLM may lose important items in the middle. 3. `action` field is not enum-validated (§1.4), so hallucinated actions pass through. |
| **Unnecessary RAG?** | No unused vector stores or embedding calls found. The system correctly avoids over-engineering this layer. |

> **Verdict**: The "RAG" layer is correctly implemented as **context grounding** and should **NOT** be replaced with vector search for this use case.

